hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15571","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Razin, from Amr ibn Umm Maktum, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I was blind, far of house, with a guide who does not suit me, so do you find for me a license to pray in my house? He said: Do you hear the call? He said: I said: Yes. He said: I find no license for you."
"15572","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muslim, narrated to us: al-Husayn narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Ibn Umm Maktum, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the mosque and saw thinness in the people and said: I intend to appoint an imam for the people, then go out and find no man lagging from prayer in his house but I burn it upon him. Ibn Umm Maktum said: O Messenger of Allah, between me and the mosque are palms and trees, and I cannot afford a guide every hour, does it allow me to pray in my house? He said: Do you hear the iqamah? He said: Yes. He said: Then come to it."
